OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNatural vision: how
OL,4,CAttenborough shaped the colourful
OL,5,Cfuture of British TV
OL,6,
OL,7,FAs Controller of BBC Two he took a lot
OL,8,Fof the creative decisions about how
OL,9,Fcolour television should develop.
OL,11,FTwo of the decisions he played an
OL,12,Fimportant part in ` and which he
OL,13,Farticulated to the public ` were
OL,14,Fprofound.
OL,16,FAttenborough took the view that colour
OL,17,Ftelevision was "natural television".
OL,18,FBlack and white images were a mere
OL,19,Fshadow or a vignette.
OL,21,FThis led to two interlinked creative
OL,22,Fpolicies.
OL,23,APub: 03-May-2026Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12203
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNatural vision: how
OL,4,CAttenborough shaped the colourful
OL,5,Cfuture of British TV
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe first was that as many BBC Two
OL,8,Fprogrammes as possible should be in
OL,9,Fcolour.
OL,11,FRather than reserve colour for special
OL,12,Fevents or spectaculars ` as was often
OL,13,Fthe case in the USA at the time ` the
OL,14,Fdecision was taken to make black and
OL,15,Fwhite programmes the exception.
OL,17,FProgrammes were only made in black and
OL,18,Fwhite because resources were
OL,19,Funavailable or for truly exceptional
OL,20,Freasons.
OL,23,APub: 03-May-2026Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12204
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNatural vision: how
OL,4,CAttenborough shaped the colourful
OL,5,Cfuture of British TV
OL,6,
OL,7,FThis is why programmes like Play
OL,8,FSchool, Newsroom and Late Night Line Up
OL,9,Fwere made in colour as quickly as
OL,10,Fpossible.
OL,12,FThe other decision was about the role
OL,13,Fcolour should play in the aesthetics of
OL,14,Fa production.
OL,16,FAgain the view was that no programme
OL,17,Fshould rely on colour for its appeal.
OL,18,FColour enhanced programmes but the
OL,19,Fprogramme still had to make sense for
OL,20,Fthe majority watching in black and
OL,21,Fwhite.
OL,23,APub: 03-May-2026Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12205
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNatural vision: how
OL,4,CAttenborough shaped the colourful
OL,5,Cfuture of British TV
OL,6,
OL,7,FIt is easy to take all this for granted
OL,8,Fnow.
OL,10,FOf course, every programme would have
OL,11,Fended up in colour eventually. But
OL,12,Fthere was no inevitability that this
OL,13,Fwould have happened in 1968 or 69 when
OL,14,Ffew had colour sets.
OL,16,FThe urge to avoid the overuse of colour
OL,17,Fin productions was also prescient.
OL,23,APub: 03-May-2026Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12206
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCNatural vision: how
OL,4,CAttenborough shaped the colourful
OL,5,Cfuture of British TV
OL,6,
OL,7,FUndoubtedly there were a few examples
OL,8,Fof designers overusing colour `
OL,9,Fespecially in light entertainment. But
OL,10,Fin general BBC colour programmes
OL,11,Favoided being garish.
OL,13,FNo doubt this all helped dispel some of
OL,14,Fthe myths which were put around about
OL,15,Fcolour TV in the early days.
OL,17,FIf the picture was bad, it was almost
OL,18,Fcertainly because of a poor signal or a
OL,19,Fbadly adjusted colour saturation
OL,20,Fcontrol.
OL,23,APub: 03-May-2026Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
